From a1d8472087ed5a65a8c6d2fe9e906f6d8ff84b5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/43] usb_webcam: show the UVC controls the camera has

The parameter web read every control as two bytes, whatever its real
size, and "Hue Auto" switched the automatic white balance
temperature instead.

The controls now come from the table in UVCControls.h: only those
the bmControls fields of the processing unit and the camera terminal
announce appear, each read with its own size and with the range and
step the camera reports. A control with two values becomes a switch,
the power line frequency a choice. Values are clamped to the range
before they are written, and every control transfer checks the
length it moved. The exposure controls of the camera terminal are
new; "Allow Lower Frame Rate" is the auto exposure priority, which
explains low frame rates in the dark.

Tested with the C920 (12 controls) and the built-in camera of a
ThinkPad T470s (13 controls).

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit b3a51dc035674ae29e724a6a45a5fcc3b149477e)
